# The key that signs muster releases (MUS-110), in ssh-keygen's allowed-signers format:
#
#   muster-release namespaces="muster-release" <key type> <public key>
#
# scripts/install-codex.sh and scripts/setup.sh carry the same lines in ALLOWED_SIGNERS, since a
# script piped from curl has no checkout to read this file from; scripts/test-install-codex.sh
# checks the three agree. scripts/sign-release.sh signs a draft release's SHA256SUMS with the
# private half, which stays with the operator.
#
# There is no key yet, so nothing verifies and both installers refuse a signed release's binaries
# (fail closed) until the operator adds the public key line here and in both scripts.
